# Handbook Chapter Structure

Every individual pattern chapter (files under `part-2-pattern-families/`, and
anything generated via `create-chapter.md`) must follow this exact structure,
in this exact order. Do not skip or reorder sections.

```markdown
# <Pattern Name>

## Purpose

## Recognition Clues

## Mental Model

## Visualization

## Generic Template

## Complexity

## Common Mistakes

## Classic Interview Questions

## Engineering Connections

## Summary
```

Section notes:

- **Purpose** — one paragraph: what real problem does this pattern solve?
- **Recognition Clues** — bullet list of interview phrasing that signals this
  pattern ("longest substring", "top K", "connected components")
- **Mental Model** — the intuition, in plain language, before any code
- **Visualization** — see `diagrams.mdc`
- **Generic Template** — language-independent pseudocode only, never a
  specific programming language
- **Complexity** — time AND space, each with a one-line justification
- **Common Mistakes** — mistakes beginners actually make, not hypothetical ones
- **Classic Interview Questions** — exactly 3 easy, 3 medium, 2 hard
- **Engineering Connections** — a real production system that uses this pattern
- **Summary** — 3-5 bullet takeaways, no new information

Target length per chapter: **~800–1,200 words** plus diagrams.

Full family files (`family-N-*.md`) contain multiple pattern sections back to
back, each following this structure independently.
